# Keep the committed bytes of every path.
#
# skit has byte-exact contracts. `tests/corpus/` is byte-exact input, and four of its files carry
# CRLF on purpose. `benchmarks/budgets.toml` must match what the renderer writes. Git rewrites line
# endings at checkout when a host sets `core.autocrlf`, and Windows runners set it. `-text` turns
# that rewrite off for every path, so a working tree holds the same bytes on every platform.
* -text
